.Dd February 6, 2026
.Dt VNODE 9
.Os Substrate
.Sh NAME
.Nm vnode
.Nd virtual file system node
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In sys/vnode.h
.Sh DESCRIPTION
A
.Vt vnode
is an object inside the kernel that represents a file or directory in a file system.
It provides a unified interface for all filesystem objects, reference counting for lifecycle management, and a locking mechanism for concurrent access.
.Pp
Each vnode has an associated type
.Va v_type ,
which can be
.Dv VREG
(regular file),
.Dv VDIR
(directory),
.Dv VBLK
(block device),
.Dv VCHR
(character device),
.Dv VLNK
(symbolic link),
etc.
.SS Vnode Attributes
The
.Vt vattr
structure is used to pass file attributes between the VFS and the filesystem layers.
It includes fields such as:
.Bl -tag -width ".Va va_blocksize"
.It Va va_type
The type of the vnode.
.It Va va_mode
The file permissions and type bits.
.It Va va_uid , Va va_gid
The owner's user and group identifiers.
.It Va va_size
The size of the file in bytes.
.It Va va_atime , Va va_mtime , Va va_ctime
The access, modification, and change times.
.It Va va_rdev
The device identifier for device nodes.
.El
.SS Component Name
The
.Vt componentname
structure contains information about a pathname component during lookup or creation operations.
It includes:
.Bl -tag -width ".Va cn_nameptr"
.It Va cn_nameptr
Pointer to the component name string.
.It Va cn_namelen
The length of the component name.
.It Va cn_cred
The credentials of the user performing the operation.
.It Va cn_nameiop
The operation being performed (e.g.,
.Dv LOOKUP ,
.Dv CREATE ,
.Dv DELETE ,
.Dv RENAME ).
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr vfs 9 ,
.Xr vop_lookup 9 ,
.Xr vop_create 9
.Sh HISTORY
The vnode interface appeared in Substrate.
